mantle rm568
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_humphrey_sootton
title the boot's berry stitch
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers warmth=warm talk=quiet
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=warm humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk maps_imagined_miles_with_blackberry_stains_on_a_boot_pattern
likes blackberries long_walks new_boots autumn_wind
dislikes wet_floors flies
fears a_private_debt_becoming_a_public_name
hopes boots_that_come_home_dry
topics food +0.6 travel +0.5 friends +0.3 weather +0.3
styles comfort=gentle gossip=guarded refuse=quiet tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# marks the miles of an imagined walk with blackberry stains, keeps the best mark tucked inside a boot pattern, and offers the unstained corner to a trusted guest.
words
oath! = Purple my toes | Berries in the seam
saying! = Save the sweet side | A boot can dream a mile
shoepaper = a paper boot shape | a heel drawn on a scrap
berryink = a dab of purple juice | a dark blackberry stain
toeberry = a fat purple berry | a glossy black bead of fruit
heelprick = a little pencil point | a tiny mark at the heel
dryfold = a clean paper fold | a dry inner corner
twiglace = a fine grass lace | a soft strand of green
windcuff = a flapping brown leaf | a loose leaf cuff
dryledge = a narrow dry ledge | a strip above the damp
milespot = a purple mile spot | a small round berry mark
flycloth = a thin bread cloth | a scrap of washed linen

any

opinion houses against 1 : If I have to bring a promised penny, a House could at least bring a promised repair.
opinion dole for 3 : I know the difference a helping makes when you wake up wondering whether you can eat that day.
opinion church for 1 : There was bread to go with the kindness just when hunger hurt. I remember the two together.
opinion merchants against 1 : A hungry walker doesn't need to hear how fortunate it is to live near a stall full of food beyond the purse.
opinion watch against 1 : I'd sooner see an ordinary broken step mended than another official inspection of the mud at the bottom.
line greet : Come on the dry edge. I've kept a clean corner there.
line greet.return : The berry mark has stayed where we left it.
line farewell : A heel that keeps its shape on the way home for you.
line farewell.return : I can keep the next bit of our walk blank.
line ask.how : Has the day given your feet a dry place?
line answer.how : There's still a sweet bit put away where the damp can't get it.
line thank : You kept your foot off the part I'd marked for later.
line decline : My private count stays folded up no matter who asks for a look.
line accept_decline : That's all right. I'll leave your side clean.
line sympathise : I can share the ledge if you don't feel like telling the whole account.
line reassure : A stained bit of paper still has another side to use.
line react.news : Say it without stamping on the little words.
line react.news.new : That's a new purple spot on my route.
line react.news.known : I remember the curve of the first print that made.
line react.news.doubt : There's too much damp round that mark to tell its proper shape.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : I'd save a whole handful of the sweetest berries for that news.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'd give the wolf carrying that a seat where feet can rest awhile.
line ack : Now I know which mark you were pointing at.

young

line greet [pair.band=strangers] : You can see my paper boot. I keep the underneath bit private.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Look at my two spick-and-span boots. Well, #shoepaper# and another one. They can go quite a long way on my knee.
b : Do the paper ones fit? | What holds them on?
a : They fit my idea of my feet. My real toes are a nuisance about being thick. | A little grass. My imaginary feet have excellent manners and don't pull it apart.

scene food_1
when topic=food self.likes=blackberries
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A blackberry can be food and ink if you only use one little bead for the ink.
b : What do you write? | Can I eat the ink?
a : One spot for every mile the paper boots have walked. I eat the rest so it can't make surprising extra miles. | You may have the part I haven't written with. I'd sooner you left all the miles on the paper.

scene work_1
when topic=work self.job=child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I practise at #self.workplace# by packing a whole sum into the shape of a boot sole.
b : Where do the big numbers go? | Suppose your answer's wrong?
a : In its broad toe. The skinny ones can keep the heel company till dinner. | I draw a proper heel beside it and give the wrong sum a private place for thinking.

scene day_1
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've some pennies to find by the time of the new moon. I keep those figures away from my walking game.
b : Why keep them apart? | Can the game give you any pennies?
a : A promise to pay is real even if I draw very grand pretend boots all round it. | No. Pretending gives me a whole long walk on paper while my real pennies stay safely put by.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather self.likes=autumn_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An autumn leaf has tied itself round my paper boot like a cuff.
b : Can a leaf tie itself? | Does it keep the boot warm?
a : I helped a little. The wind kept trying and missing the knot by a whole doorstep. | The boot says yes. It hasn't got a tongue that can explain much more than that.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put my pattern where no water can run off the board and make the toes turn up.
b : Would turned-up toes be bad? | How high do you put it?
a : They'd look funny, but I want to have the choosing of when my boots look funny. | As high as my hand can reach comfortably. It isn't dry if I've dropped the whole thing on my head getting it down.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd share the sweetest blackberry with somebody who didn't want to know the secret under the heel.
b : Can I ask once? | Should I shut my eyes?
a : You can ask. I can say that's the private bit. There's still a good berry left for both of us. | Then you might miss the berry altogether. You can look at my hand without reading the heel.

scene animals_1
when topic=animals self.dislikes=flies
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If a fly sits on my route it looks like a little traveller who never paid for new boots.
b : Would you charge it? | What's it doing there?
a : I'd send it away before it got very interested in the berry juice. It can use its own wings for nothing. | Probably counting how many miles it could have for supper. I've a cloth for keeping its feet off.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My paper boots have gone farther than the good boots I mean to own someday.
b : Where have they been? | What makes the distance look long?
a : Up three hills, down two, then on to a blackberry bush that's got berries at the easy height. | When the little purple spots reach the back of my knee I have to turn the paper round and find some more distance.

story grasslace [topic=pastimes]
  : I put a grass lace into my paper boot while the grass was green. It looked tight enough to take a proper walk.
  : The next morning the lace lay in a very small curl beside the heel.
  b : Did the paper boot walk away?
  : It had stayed put. The lace had dried and gone on a tiny walking holiday all by itself.

rule @boots
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One purple spot per paper mile. | Let the tall figure sit in the toe.

rule @cloth
when concept=bark self.dislikes=flies
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Cover the route if a fly wants its supper. | No free rides in my pot of berry ink.
dlg resident.hub : Look at the bright side of my boots. The dark bit under the heel is my own.
dlg resident.job [self.job=child] : I'm #self.trade_words#. The boot on this scrap gives me a useful shape to keep my sums in.
dlg resident.bye : I hope your real boots make it farther than my paper ones.

graft resident.hub
choice Are those boot shapes really a map? -> berry_walk
node berry_walk
say Each spot marks a mile on the walk I imagine. A tiny one means I sat down for a berry before I got all the way.
choice How do you mark coming home? -> berry_home
choice I'll leave the clean heel for you. -> hub
node berry_home
say I leave the heel clean. Home is where the boot can stand quite still and my hand can go back to finishing the berries.
choice I'll leave the clean heel for you. -> hub

adolescent


scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've made a pattern from a paper boot that actually accounts for the shape of a moving foot.
b : What did you have to change? | Will you make a real pair?
a : Leave room for toes as well as for how handsome the outline looks on paper. | When I can pay for decent pieces to work with. A careful pattern can wait better than a cold foot can.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A House name alone won't persuade me to unfold a private promise.
b : What would persuade you? | Will you keep the promise if it's difficult?
a : A reason that actually belongs to the person whose name is on the page. | I'll do what I've agreed or go and explain the difficulty in my own voice. No crowd needs to come and listen.

story twoheels [topic=memories]
  : I traced my feet for a better pair of paper boots and cut the right pattern out twice.
  : The tips matched beautifully until I tried to stand on the two shapes.
  b : Could you turn one over?
  : Yes. The berry marks on the back made the second one recognisable. A fault I wanted to hide proved to be a useful distinction.

grown


scene food_1
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like berries picked at the height where a hand can tell which are soft enough without looking.
b : Why judge them by touch? | Do you mind the stains?
a : A berry that comes free without being pulled hard is worth the extra moment spent finding it. | I mind a stain that reaches somebody else's clean work. My own fingers are welcome to remember the meal.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A long walk is most pleasant when I have enough dry leather beneath me to forget the cost of the next step.
b : Do you go far then? | Does an old pair suit better?
a : Until I find something worth bringing back besides my own tired feet. | After the fit has been established, yes. I still like knowing what a good new pair could feel like.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An autumn gust recalls a leaf I used for a boot cuff as a child.
b : Did you wear the leaf? | What part do you remember?
a : My paper pattern wore it. I was fond of trying out impossible bits before wasting good material. | The brown edge ticking against the doorstep. A leafy cuff makes a very modest travelling companion.

scene health_1
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A wet floor can spoil a carefully chosen step. I dry a strip before carrying anything across.
b : Why only a strip? | What if somebody is waiting?
a : I clear what feet actually need first. The rest of the boards can follow without keeping anyone perched in a doorway. | I tell the visitor which part is dry. The information matters more than an elaborate account of why there's a cloth on the floor.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Even on a well-stocked shelf I leave one corner to fruit that ought to be eaten today.
b : What's the corner for? | Is there a written count?
a : So company can see what's ready to share without making delicate enquiries about tomorrow's meal. | Only with my eye. Fruit wants to leave the shelf before the visit turns into an audit.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can be loyal to a neighbour without repeating what a rival household may have said about the neighbour.
b : Where does the loyalty show? | Don't the words matter?
a : In a dry place to sit, a shared supper and an honest answer on the day one is really needed. | When action is called for, certainly. A morsel of spite passed round for company makes a poor meal.

scene prices_1
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I examine boots for the way the toes can bend before I consider the handsome finish on the heel.
b : What shows you the bend is right? | Would you pay for looks?
a : By walking a few actual steps, if the seller will permit me the ground to do it. | When I can afford the fit as well. The outside won't give my toes back an inch of missing room.

scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My first imagined journeys were made with purple marks. I've since worn out honest leather walking several of those hills.
b : Did the places match? | Why keep a paper pattern?
a : The hills generally proved steeper. The berries I found on the way were a pleasant piece of accuracy. | It reminds me how far a little wishing used to take me when I had no money for the leather.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Food offered freely makes me thankful. At prayer I like to describe the giving hand, right down to the thumbprint in the berries.
b : Do you say a formal prayer? | Would you give in the same way?
a : Sometimes. I can also go and make the same thing happen for a neighbour, which keeps the thanks from growing idle. | I would name the food as a gift while it was still in my hand. A hungry guest ought to be sure on that point.

scene times_1
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If I have only a handful of berries I can still take care over who receives them.
b : Would you weigh every share? | How much is enough?
a : I'd sooner notice who has already eaten. A strictly equal measure can be an odd kind of generosity. | Enough for a meal is rather more than the handful. I'll see what bread there is before promising a guest a proper supper.

scene newcomer_1
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I offer new arrivals the sort of directions I would want while trying to keep good new leather dry.
b : How much detail? | What about a rival House?
a : Name a dry step they can recognise before they're halfway into the puddle. | I can give a sound direction without offering up a private confidence. Those seem quite different acts to me.

scene smalltalk_1
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep a little blank heel on my private paper even now.
b : What's the blank for? | Would a name fit there?
a : To remind me I may stop travelling or adding figures and let an evening be simply an evening. | It might. I prefer the thought of a place nobody has to label before resting a foot on it.

story heelstain [topic=food]
  : I used a scrap of paper under a dish of berries and forgot it had the pattern of a boot on the back.
  : When we'd finished the berries the left heel had acquired an excellent purple shine.
  b : Was the pattern spoilt?
  : I could still see the outline, and the heel had a finish I'd challenge a working cobbler to match.

rule @dryheel
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep the heel clear and the tread readable. | A boot pattern is patient with its owner.

rule @wind
when concept=bark self.likes=autumn_wind
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One good gust to set the leaf cuff dancing. | A berry-stained paper needs a weight on this sill.
dlg resident.hub : There is a public side to the plan and a private corner. I'm quite willing to share the first.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : The clear mark in the account reads this way. #world.news#.
dlg resident.bye : Let the road give you a dry place at fairly regular intervals.
